COMMANDS
echo > file    echo >> file
sort    uniq    uniq -c    wc -l
cmd1 | cmd2    2> file

SYMBOLS
>     replace the whole file
>>    add a new line at the end
|     hand the output to the next command
2>    send errors to a file

LEARNED
- cp to a name that doesn't exist makes a file, not a folder
- git add picks the changes, git commit saves them
- uniq only removes neighbouring repeats, so sort first
- Normal output (1) and errors (2) are separate;
  > only catches normal output
- Relative paths start where I am, so check the prompt
- Spaces split a command; cp's last item is the destination

